# /etc/onceroot/rules: what onceroot does before it asks anyone.
#
#   allow|deny <absolute program path> [<argument pattern>...] [...]
#
# First match wins. A pattern is a literal or ends in * (prefix match).
# A trailing ... lets further arguments through; without it the number of
# arguments must match exactly. No match means: ask a person.
# Shells, interpreters, command wrappers, privilege tools and editors are
# denied by onceroot itself and no rule here can allow them.

# Read-only queries run without asking. Prefer exact arguments: a trailing
# ... lets any further flags through, and some tools take flags that change
# state (journalctl --vacuum-*, for one), so never end an allow rule with ...
# for a tool unless every flag it accepts is read-only.
allow /usr/bin/pacman -Q* ...
allow /usr/bin/systemctl status ...

# Never, whoever asks.
deny /usr/bin/pacman -R* ...
